<title>CHINA: China cashmere exports seen up slightly in 1997.</title>
<headline>China cashmere exports seen up slightly in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>China is expected to export slightly more cashmere in 1997 than the estimated 2,300 tonnes shipped out of the country last year, the Overseas Edition of the People's Daily said on Monday.</p>
<p>Exports would be boosted by the implementation of strict public bidding and the removal of export controls, but the increase was unlikely to be big, the newspaper said but gave no figures.</p>
<p>Cashmere supplies and prices on the domestic market would be relatively stable in 1997, although processing capacity would continue to far exceed production, it said.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
